.SH NAME
evolve-login - Sign in to a patchy remote-evaluation service.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBevolve login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in to a patchy remote-evaluation service.

.PP
The service advertises its OIDC issuer and client id (GET /api/v1/auth/info),
so the only configuration is the service URL itself: --remote-url, or the
remote.url config key (env EVOLVE_REMOTE_URL). The flow is authorization-code
with PKCE against a public client — no client secret anywhere — redirecting to
an ephemeral localhost listener; a browser opens best-effort and the URL is
always printed for the times it cannot.

.PP
The credential is stored per remote URL in the user configuration directory
(evolve/credentials.json), not in any repository.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--no-browser\fP[=false]
	print the sign-in URL only; never launch a browser

.PP
\fB--remote-url\fP=""
	patchy remote-evaluation service URL (default: the remote.url config key)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit machine-readable JSONL progress on stdout

.PP
\fB--layout\fP="auto"
	repository layout: auto, marketplace, multi, or single

.PP
\fB--results-format\fP=""
	format for results files and the EVALUATION rollup: json, jsonc, or yaml (default: config results_format or json)

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	repository root to operate on (default: walk up from the current directory)

.PP
\fB--telemetry-dir\fP=""
	write OpenTelemetry traces/metrics/logs as JSON to this directory (default: off; overrides OTEL_* env vars)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug logging


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBevolve(1)\fP
